# Your board's settings. Copy to .env (git-ignored, chmod 600) and fill in; nothing here is printed,
# logged or committed. Leave a line empty to keep its default.

# --- Device: Wi-Fi -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read only by `tools/set_wifi.py --env` (tools/flash.sh runs it after flashing), which sends them to the
# board over USB; they end up only on the board and never in the build. The board joins home Wi-Fi first
# and falls back to the iPhone hotspot when home is out of reach. 2.4 GHz only; passwords 8-63
# characters, or empty for an open network. Either pair may be blank.

# Home Wi-Fi
WAVESHARE_AI_WIFI_SSID=
WAVESHARE_AI_WIFI_PASSWORD=

# iPhone Personal Hotspot: the name is the iPhone's name (Settings > General > About > Name) and the
# password is under Settings > Personal Hotspot > Wi-Fi Password. Turn on Maximize Compatibility
# there so the hotspot uses 2.4 GHz, which this board needs.
WAVESHARE_AI_HOTSPOT_SSID=
WAVESHARE_AI_HOTSPOT_PASSWORD=

# --- Device: battery ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by dev.sh (rebuild to change). On battery, go to sleep after this many minutes without a touch
# or a button press, 0..120. 0 or empty = never (the power button and BOOT always sleep/wake).
WAVESHARE_AI_AUTO_SLEEP_MIN=

# --- Providers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by dev.sh (rebuild to change).
# Which providers to build, comma-separated: hermes (Sparkles + Ask, sign-in through your auth gateway),
# home_assistant (the Sensor tile with its own sign-in), or none (the device core only).
# Empty = hermes only. PROVIDERS=... on the dev.sh command line overrides this for one build.
WAVESHARE_AI_PROVIDERS=
# Which Hermes tiles to build, comma-separated: sparkles, ask. Empty = both.
WAVESHARE_AI_HERMES_TILES=
# The sign-in name on the Hermes tab in Settings ("<name>: signed in as ..."), 1-16 characters.
# Empty = Hermes.
WAVESHARE_AI_HERMES_ACCOUNT_NAME=
# The same for the Home Assistant tab, 1-16 characters. Empty = Home Assistant.
WAVESHARE_AI_HOME_ASSISTANT_ACCOUNT_NAME=
